source: tests/help_pages.rs
description: "a command's -h and --help pages as this build renders them at 100 columns without color; any change to an about, a flag, a value, a heading or the layout changes them: review with cargo insta review, or re-accept with INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test --test integration help_pages:: and review git diff tests/snapshots/"
---
==> omaddons install -h <==
Install or update addons on one client

Usage: omaddons install [OPTIONS] <REF>...
Aliases: add

Arguments:
  <REF>...  What to install: a catalog name, a ref, a link or a local path

Options:
      --channel <CHANNEL>  The release channel to install from [possible values: stable, beta,
                           alpha]
      --version <VERSION>  Install exactly this release: a tag for gh: refs, a rev for git: refs
      --file <ZIP>         Install this downloaded archive as the release of the one given ref
      --reinstall          Install the recorded release again, replacing its folders
      --no-deps            Install only the named addons, not the ones their TOCs require
      --force              Take over another addon's folder, or replace an unmanaged one
      --strict             Exit 6 when only some of the addons install
      --refresh            Fetch every release from its source, never from remembered metadata
      --any-flavor         Install builds the publisher did not make for this client
      --no-any-flavor      Clear --any-flavor for these addons on this client

Examples:
  omaddons install dbm bigwigs -t retail  catalog names, in one transaction
  omaddons install gh:tullamods/OmniCC --dry-run
                                          preview it, and store the plan
  omaddons install ./MyAddon.zip -t era   a local zip or folder

Global: -t <TARGET>  --json  --dry-run  -v  --quiet  --no-color  --offline  (--help lists them all)
==> omaddons install --help <==
Install or update addons on one client

Each ref is verified by the client's own TOC rules before anything is written, and one transaction
installs them all, undoable.

Usage: omaddons install [OPTIONS] <REF>...
Aliases: add

Arguments:
  <REF>...
          What to install: a catalog name, a ref, a link or a local path
          
          A catalog name (weakauras), owner/repo, a canonical ref (gh:, git:, url:, file:, wowi:,
          tukui:, wowace:), a pasted GitHub or https link, or a path to a zip or folder.

Options:
      --channel <CHANNEL>
          The release channel to install from
          
          Default: the addon's recorded channel, then default_channel, then stable.
          
          [possible values: stable, beta, alpha]

      --version <VERSION>
          Install exactly this release: a tag for gh: refs, a rev for git: refs

      --file <ZIP>
          Install this downloaded archive as the release of the one given ref

      --reinstall
          Install the recorded release again, replacing its folders
          
          It repairs modified or missing files, undoably.

      --no-deps
          Install only the named addons, not the ones their TOCs require

      --force
          Take over another addon's folder, or replace an unmanaged one
          
          Take over a folder another addon owns or an addon of the same name from another ref, or
          replace an unmanaged folder; undoable until retention prunes the snapshot.

      --strict
          Exit 6 when only some of the addons install

      --refresh
          Fetch every release from its source, never from remembered metadata

      --any-flavor
          Install builds the publisher did not make for this client
          
          Recorded on the addon there: every later update and sync keeps it, until --no-any-flavor.

      --no-any-flavor
          Clear --any-flavor for these addons on this client

Examples:
  omaddons install dbm bigwigs -t retail  catalog names, in one transaction
  omaddons install gh:tullamods/OmniCC --dry-run
                                          preview it, and store the plan
  omaddons install ./MyAddon.zip -t era   a local zip or folder

An addon is installed from one ref at a time. Another local archive of a local
install (./Bar-2.2.0.zip over ./Bar-2.1.0.zip) updates it; an addon of the same
name from any other ref is a takeover, refused (ownership_conflict) unless --force.

See also: search, apply, undo

Global options:
      --json              One JSON envelope on stdout
      --format <FORMAT>   Output format [possible values: json, human]
  -t, --target <TARGET>   The client to act on: id, game mode, family, path, or all [alias:
                          --flavor]
      --dry-run           Show the plan without changing anything
      --actor <ACTOR>     Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]
      --reason <TEXT>     Why, recorded verbatim in history
      --offline           Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]
      --while-running     Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)
      --if-match <TOKEN>  Run only what the preview that returned this token showed
      --no-color          No ANSI color
      --no-progress       No progress output
      --progress <MODE>   Progress events on stderr [possible values: json, human, none]
      --quiet             Only errors on stderr
  -v, --verbose...        More detail (repeatable)
  -h, --help              Show help

Learn more: omaddons robot-docs guide
